course: dictionary
lesson: 9980
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. You can tell which meaning an author means by reading the words around it. That context is your clue. A «brain teaser» is a puzzle, so the word before it, brain, and the idea of thinking hard tell you what teaser means here.
explain: A teaser can also be a short preview, like a clip or advert that shows a little of something so you want to see more. Check each meaning by putting it into the sentence. Does a puzzle, a preview or a person fit best?
explain: The third meaning is a person who teases others. «Making fun of someone's accident is unkind, and it is the teaser who is in the wrong.» The words unkind and in the wrong show that a teaser is someone who makes fun of others in a hurtful way.
explain: Teasing can be playful or hurtful. «You and Sophie sitting in a tree» is a teasing playground rhyme, and if it goes on, you should tell an adult. Nicknames often fade when the person stops reacting, so staying calm can help.
fact: A teaser is a short puzzle or question that makes you think hard, often called a brain teaser.
fact: A teaser can be a short preview, like a clip or advert, that makes you curious about something.
fact: A teaser can also be a person who teases others, often in a playful or unkind way.
fact: A «teaser trailer» gives a small look at a new film so that people want to see the whole thing.
fact: Nicknames often fade when the person stops reacting, and getting angry usually makes teasers say them more.
exercise: In maths, a «brain teaser» is a | A person who sits at the back | A cold drink | A long book about numbers | *A short puzzle that makes you think hard
exercise: «The film's teaser trailer gave us a tiny look at the new film.» What is a teaser here? | A kind of film camera | A person who makes fun of others | A puzzle to solve | *A short preview
exercise: «Making fun of someone's body is unkind, and it is the teaser who is in the wrong.» What is a teaser here? | A short puzzle | A short preview | *A person who teases others | A friendly guide
test: Which word fits? «Nicknames often fade when the person stops reacting; getting angry usually makes ___ say them more.» | previews | trailers | *teasers | puzzles
test: Find the meaning: «Can you solve this brain teaser?» Teaser here means | A playground rhyme | A person who teases | *A puzzle that makes you think | A clip of a new film
exam: «You and Sophie sitting in a tree» is a teasing playground rhyme. Which meaning of teaser fits best here? | A short preview | *A person who teases others | A short puzzle | A kind of tree
